      "dom_id": "step-q221699",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Consider the following false statement.\n\n$5n-2>3$ for any $n\\in Z.$ \n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,5n-2>3.\n$$\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,5n-2>3)\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,5n-2\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n5n-2\\le 3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
